# Navigation Architecture

## Screen model

Navigation is a discriminated union held in `App.tsx` state. There is no router library.

```ts
type Screen =
  | { id: 'home' }
  | { id: 'lists' }
  | { id: 'edit-pack-list'; listId: string | null }  // null = new list
  | { id: 'new-packing' }
  | { id: 'packing'; packingId: string }
```

## Rules

- `App.tsx` owns the `screen` state and passes `onNavigate` down to screens.
- Screens never import each other. Navigation is always upward via `onNavigate`.
- Back navigation is always available on every screen except `home`.
- The home screen is the only screen that shows the global active-packings overview.
- No deep linking or URL-based routing is needed — this is an offline-first PWA.

## Data flow

- Each screen loads its own data from IndexedDB on mount via `useEffect`.
- Screens pass minimal IDs (not full objects) to child screens via the navigation union.
- After a mutation, screens reload from DB to stay in sync.
